# React / TSX Components

These files are islands inside an Astro site. Keep them small and typed.

- Use functional components and named `Props` interfaces. Do not use class components or `any`.
- Import content types from `astro:content` (e.g. `CollectionEntry<"blog">`) instead of duplicating post shapes.
- Use existing path aliases (`@utils`, `@config`, `@components`) rather than long relative imports.
- Style with Tailwind classes already used on the site (`text-skin-accent`, `decoration-dashed`). Do not add a CSS module or styled-components.
- Prefer composition over new dependencies. This project only uses React where interactivity is needed (cards, search, datetime).

```tsx
// ❌ BAD
export default function Card(props: any) {
  return <div>{props.frontmatter.title}</div>;
}

// ✅ GOOD
export interface Props {
  frontmatter: CollectionEntry<"blog">["data"];
}

export default function Card({ frontmatter }: Props) {
  return <h2 className="text-lg font-medium">{frontmatter.title}</h2>;
}
```
